theory.intro:
The **distance** between two points is the length of the interval joining them. That interval is the hypotenuse of a right-angled triangle whose legs are the **run** and the **rise**, so Pythagoras' theorem gives $d = \sqrt{\text{run}^2 + \text{rise}^2}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.3]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4,2.6);
\coordinate (C) at (4,0);
\draw[thick,blue] (A) -- (B) node[midway,above left,black] {$d$};
\draw[dashed,red] (A) -- (C) node[midway,below,black] {run};
\draw[dashed,red] (C) -- (B) node[midway,right,black] {rise};
\coordinate (p) at ($(C)!0.4cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (q) at ($(C)!0.4cm!(B)$);
\draw (p) -- ($(p)+(q)-(C)$) -- (q);
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

